<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Blankenburg (Harz)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Blankenburg is a town on the northern edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harz">Harz</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Seat of medieval counts, it passed to the dukes of Brunswick-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolfenbuttel">Wolfenbüttel</a>, whose junior branch made its large castle a residence and, from 1707 to 1731, the capital of the Principality of Blankenburg. Members of the ducal house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a>, among them Viktoria Luise, daughter of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-ii">Wilhelm II</a>, lived there until 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/blankenburg-harz.jpg" alt="Blankenburg (Harz)" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: JurecGermany · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blankenburg_wr.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
